,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Slice 4 of decision record 0004 (`pkgs/mcpx/docs/decisions/0004-scope-resolved-roots.md`, PR #957). Depends on slice 1 (#958) and slice 3 (#959); slice 2 not required. Related: #864 (the fleet `.mcpx.json` still carries `/home/user` absolute paths — this slice needs the config in its post-#864 shape, or must say why it proceeded anyway).\n\n## What to do\n- Flip `gopls-mcp-server` to `\"scope\": \"worktree\"` in the fleet config (the user-level config symlinked to this repo's `.mcpx.json`; identical server lists on both machines stay identical).\n- This is deliberately last: flipping scopes before the spawn-cwd and initialize work landed would only multiply processes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (live proof, from nix#817/#819)\n- [ ] With gopls at `\"scope\": \"worktree\"` behind the fixed spawn cwd and initialize root, `go_package_api` on a module path returns the module's real API promptly (the 2026-10-25 result — empty after 156 s — does not recur).\n- [ ] The same proof passes for a caller in a linked worktree, rooted in that worktree, not just the main checkout.\n- [ ] Two callers in different checkouts get distinct gopls instances, each rooted in its own checkout (visible in `mcpx status` root field from slice 1).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/961/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/961/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}